          "shortDescription" : {
            "text" : "low severity - CVE-2025-46653 Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG) vulnerability in pkg:npm/formidable@2.1.2"
          },
          "fullDescription" : {
            "text" : "Formidable (aka node-formidable) 2.1.0 through 3.x before 3.5.3 relies on hexoid to prevent guessing of filenames for untrusted executable content; however, hexoid is documented as not \"cryptographically secure.\" (Also, there is a scenario in which only the last two characters of a hexoid string need to be guessed, but this is not often relevant.) NOTE: this does not imply that, in a typical use case, attackers will be able to exploit any hexoid behavior to upload and execute their own content."
