        }, {
          "id" : "GHSA-mwcw-c2x4-8c55",
          "shortDescription" : {
            "text" : "medium severity - GHSA-mwcw-c2x4-8c55 Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop') vulnerability in pkg:npm/nanoid@3.3.3"
          },
          "fullDescription" : {
            "text" : "When nanoid is called with a fractional value, there were a number of undesirable effects:\n\n1. in browser and non-secure, the code infinite loops on while (size--)\n2. in node, the value of poolOffset becomes fractional, causing calls to nanoid to return zeroes until the pool is next filled\n3. if the first call in node is a fractional argument, the initial buffer allocation fails with an error\n\nVersion 3.3.8 and 5.0.9 are fixed."
          },
          "help" : {
            "text" : "",
