    }, {
      "ruleId" : "GHSA-mwcw-c2x4-8c55",
      "level" : "warning",
      "message" : {
        "text" : "GHSA-mwcw-c2x4-8c55 - When nanoid is called with a fractional value, there were a number of undesirable effects:\n\n1. in browser and non-secure, the code infinite loops on while (size--)\n2. in node, the value of poolOffset becomes fractional, causing calls to nanoid to return zeroes until the pool is next filled\n3. if the first call in node is a fractional argument, the initial buffer allocation fails with an error\n\nVersion 3.3.8 and 5.0.9 are fixed."
      },
      "partialFingerprints" : {
        "vulnerabilityHash" : "5cf8b51f79325bc46a2bf462219434b0"
      },
